  "comparative_synthesis": {
    "sudden_distress_vulnerability": "Across all Phase 5 standalone models (w=1, 2, 5, 10, ROS15), healthy-to-distressed recall remains strictly depressed (0/5 or 1/5). Deterioration-engineered features alone cannot detect sudden corporate default.",
    "ensemble_tradeoff": "Blending baseline and candidate models (alpha >= 0.4) restores detection of Firm 60 (+1 healthy detection, raising recall to 36.36%). However, all blended models produce 31 to 35 alerts (11.8% to 13.4%), breaching the 8% operational capacity ceiling (cap = 20).",
    "feasibility_conclusion": "No evaluated research candidate or ensemble configuration simultaneously satisfies the 8% alert budget AND matches the approved baseline's 45.45% sensitivity on the T=13->T=14 cohort."
  }
}